  "question": {
    "text": "$n$ moles of an ideal gas undergo a process $A \\rightarrow B$ as shown in the figure. Maximum temperature of the gas during the process is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5K-QnjAnePVrTyiX2jsk1Tn3reCBdq9nhssOS9kB51s.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1lN9Y",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{9 P_0 V_0}{n R}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sZOfm",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 P_0 V_0}{2 n R}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w2Icl",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{9 P_0 V_0}{2 n R}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6t8hm",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{9 P_0 V_0}{4 n R}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For given graph, equation of $P$ - $V$ line is\n$$\nP-2 P_0=\\frac{2 P_0-P_0}{V_0-2 V_0}\\left(V-V_0\\right)\n$$\nSo, $P=3 P_0-\\frac{P_0}{V_0} V$ as $P V=n R T$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow\\left(3 P_0-\\frac{P_0}{V_0} V\\right) V=n R T ;\n$$\nFor maximum temperature $\\frac{d T}{d V}=0$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{d T}{d V}=3 P_0-\\frac{2 P_0}{V_0} V=0 \\Rightarrow V=\\frac{3}{2} V_0\n$$\nAlso $P=\\frac{3}{2} P_0$\nSo, $T=\\frac{P V}{n R}=\\frac{1}{n R} \\times \\frac{3}{2} P_0 \\times \\frac{3}{2} V_0=\\frac{9 P_0 V_0}{4 n R}$",
    "image": null
  },
